<title>USA: Braun's Fashions Q4 shr profit vs loss.</title>
<headline>Braun's Fashions Q4 shr profit vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Dollars in thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>			Three Months Ended</p>
<p>			     March 1, 1997	March 2, 1996</p>
<p>			    Thirteen Weeks    Fourteen Weeks</p>
<p> Net sales		   $24,511		$26,380</p>
<p> Net income (loss)	 $ 4,304		$(1,952)</p>
<p> Net income (loss) shr   $  0.90		$ (0.51)</p>
<p> Avg shrs			4,769		  3,793</p>
<p>			Fiscal Year Ended</p>
<p>			   March 1, 1997	March 2, 1996</p>
<p>			 Fifty-Two Weeks   Fifty-Three Weeks</p>
<p> Net sales		   $ 95,946	    $97,296</p>
<p> Net income (loss)	  $ (621)	   $ (3,458)</p>
<p> Net income (loss) shr   $ (0.15)	   $ (0.91)</p>
<p> Avg shrs			 4,029		3,792</p>
<p>Full company name is Braun's Fashions Corp  </p>
<p>NOTE: In fiscal 1996 the company recorded a valuation allowance of $1.8 million or $0.47 per share equal to the full amount of its deferred assets, due to uncertainty of realizing the value of these assets in future years.</p>
<p>In fiscal 1997, it reversed the valuation allowance due to recent operating performance and recorded another $255,000 of deferred tax assets. Current fourth quarter includes a $2.4 million one-time gain mostly due to the deferred tax and reorganization adjustments.</p>
<p>New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
